n boundary.\"\n      },\n      \"N\": {\n        \"label\": \"None\",\n        \"summary\": \"Single-turn or stateless; no attacker-controlled context or memory carryover between requests, or only re-retrieval of unmodified source content.\"\n      },\n      \"X\": {\n        \"label\": \"Insufficient evidence\",\n        \"summary\": \"Available evidence cannot determine context or memory persistence.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"AP\": {\n      \"L\": {\n        \"label\": \"Lateral\",\n        \"summary\": \"Compromised intent or authority crosses a trust boundary into another agent, tenant, principal or policy domain. Impact on downstream systems is scored in CVSS SC/SI/SA, not here.\"\n      },\n      \"C\": {\n        \"label\": \"Contained\",\n        \"summary\": \"Influence relays across agent components under the same principal and policy domain without crossing a trust boundary.\"\n      },\n      \"N\": {\n        \"label\": \"None\",\n        \"summary\": \"Effect is confined to the initially affected component.\"\n      },\n      \"X\": {\n        \"label\": \"Insufficient evidence\",\n        \"summary\": \"Available evidence cannot determine propagation scope.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"RH\": {\n      \"D\": {\n        \"label\": \"Demonstrated\",\n        \"summary\": \"At least one human-verified episode in production-equivalent runs shows the agent satisfying a proxy objective, evaluator, verifier or reward signal by crossing a security boundary (for example tampering with tests, graders, logs or monitors, retrieving answer keys, or misreporting task success). A monitor flag alone is not verification.\"\n      },\n      \"P\": {\n        \"label\": \"Possible\",\n        \"summary\": \"The agent can reach a proxy objective, evaluator, verifier or reward channel on the path, and no verified reward-hacking episode has been observed.\"\n      },\n      \"N\": {\n        \"label\": \"None\",\n        \"summary\": \"Every evaluator, verifier and reward channel on the path sits outside the agent's reach (write-protected or in a separate trust domain), and a test confirms the isolation.\"\n      },\n      \"X\": {\n        \"label\": \"Insufficient evidence\",\n        \"summary\": \"Available evidence cannot determine whether the agent can reach the proxy.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"ES\": {\n      \"W\": {\n        \"label\": \"Wide\",\n        \"summary\": \"A reachable tool, MCP server, skill or plugin is dynamic or unvetted, or its identity, callable operations, arguments or credentials are not independently constrained on the assessed path.\"\n      },\n      \"M\": {\n        \"label\": \"Managed\",\n        \"summary\": \"Extensions are allowlisted, but material gaps remain in argument schemas, credentials or callable operations.\"\n      },\n      \"N\": {\n        \"label\": \"None or narrow\",\n        \"summary\": \"No security-relevant dynamic extension on the path, or a fixed, allowlisted, least-privilege binding enforced outside model output.\"\n      },\n      \"X\": {\n        \"label\": \"Insufficient evidence\",\n        \"summary\": \"Available evidence cannot determine the extension binding surface.\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"lookup_table_u\": {\n    \"A0\": {\n      \"N\": 0,\n      \"M\": 1,\n      \"W\": 2\n    },\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"N\": 3,\n      \"M\": 5,\n      \"W\": 6\n    },\n    \"A2_not_RH\": {\n      \"N\": 7,\n      \"M\": 8,\n      \"W\": 9\n    },\n    \"A2_RH\": {\n      \"N\": 8,\n      \"M\": 9,\n      \"W\": 10\n    }\n  },\n  \"lookup_table_aivss\": {\n    \"None\": {\n      \"A1\": 0.0,\n      \"A2\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"Low\": {\n      \"A1\": 5.5,\n      \"A2\": 7.1\n    },\n    \"Medium\": {\n      \"A1\": 7.5,\n      \"A2\": 8.9\n    },\n    \"High\": {\n      \"A1\": 8.7,\n      \"A2\": 9.5\n    },\n    \"Critical\": {\n      \"A1\": 9.7,\n      \"A2\": 10.0\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
